  "root_review": {
    "scope": "All eight production-file changes, daemon configuration, the resource Worker adapter, ownership/encoding paths, and output/HTTP regression definitions.",
    "observations": [
      "Authentication and Scope denial precede new output admission; trusted deployment/tenant and class are checked again at scheduler submission.",
      "Global/tenant charge is atomic, allocator runs outside the lock, and dynamic buffers hold their base lease.",
      "The actual Job retains WorkHold after caller timeout or failed send; final Bytes clones and slices retain the original backing charge.",
      "OwnedValue drops Value before context charges; FinalOwner takes a base reference before the old Value/context are destroyed.",
      "Query resource refusal returns LIMIT; trusted execute/Committed-resolution receipts retain COMMITTED_BUT_UNAVAILABLE; UNKNOWN and head-effect uncertainty are not upgraded.",
      "The ordinary execution path finishes JSON in its worker before the original deadline and checks it again at send; queued close paths only finalize fixed small failures.",
      "No inverse scheduler/pool lock order was found: admission releases pool locks before enqueue; output destruction never reenters the scheduler.",
      "Old unmetered public Rust APIs remain explicitly separate; the new Worker capability defaults to UNAVAILABLE and the real Engine/ObservedWorker forward it."
    ],
    "result": "No static production correctness blocker identified. This is not compiled or actual-runtime acceptance."
  },
